## study
Dr. Briefs' Study
Status:  NoQuit, NoRecall, NoPortal
Obvious exits:
South -  Family Lounge
West  -  Inner Hall
Gohan tugs at the collar of a borrowed suit, looking for somewhere quiet to read.
Emperor Pilaf mutters about a plan, a drawing of a plan.
You find a trail of light, quick footprints through spilled punch. (evidence #6)
Only dust and party streamers.
This room is done for now. Your notebook lists the rest.
Nobody was hurt tonight: the Dragon Radar was stolen. inspect cradle in the Study.
## hangar
Hangar
Status:  NoQuit, NoRecall, NoPortal
Obvious exits:
South -  Robot Workshop
Puar floats near the ceiling, nervous.
The stand-ins' party log: at nine, the Dragon Radar was still in its cradle in the Study.
Four findings: Jaco will hear an accusation now. accuse alone shows the words.
## kitchen
Kitchen
Status:  NoQuit, NoRecall, NoPortal
Obvious exits:
East  -  Inner Hall
South -  Dining Room
Yajirobe is eating something he should not be.
Tucked out of sight: a plain Hoi Poi capsule with no label, its button taped down. The thief hid the Dragon Radar in one just like it and left two more to fool you, and only Jaco can open them: name the room in your accusation. Capsules found: 1 of 3.
A capsule wrapper, a lost earring, a crumb of cake. Nothing that matters.
This room is done for now. Your notebook lists the rest.
## portraits
Four portraits hang here, left to right:
  Dr. Briefs, capsule 8
  Bulma, capsule 4
  Mrs. Briefs, capsule 5
  Trunks, capsule 2
A brass plaque below: Alphabetical, by the name on each frame.
The lab keypad takes the four numbers in that order, as one code: press 1234 style, in the Lab Vestibule.
## gravity
Gravity Chamber
Status:  NoQuit, NoRecall, NoPortal
Obvious exits:
North -  Robot Workshop
You find a tuft of something that is not dark hair. (evidence #4)
You turn the room over twice. Whatever happened tonight, it left no mark here.
This room is done for now. Your notebook lists the rest.
## attic
Attic
Status:  NoQuit, NoRecall, NoPortal
Obvious exits:
Down  -  Upper Landing West
Tucked out of sight: a black calling card stamped with a silver top hat, and on the back in neat script, With compliments, the Phantom. It has nothing to do with tonight's case and is no finding, but solve the case in time and the card is yours to keep. Your casebook counts them.
You check under every cushion and behind every frame. Nothing new.
This room is done for now. Your notebook lists the rest.
